# Acknowledgments

Ifrit's own source code is released under the Apache License 2.0 (see `LICENSE`). That license does
not cover the third-party material listed here, which is used under the license named in each entry.

This file is where credit for third-party material is recorded and kept. It gives, for each asset,
what its license asks for: who made it, where it came from, under which license, what was changed,
and which files in this repository carry it.

## Adding an asset

Before a third-party asset that requires attribution is merged (an icon, an image, a font, a
dataset, a snippet of someone else's code), add an entry below, copying the template at the end.
Do not merge the asset without it. Keep the credit in the asset's own file too where the format
allows (for example a header comment), so the notice travels with the file.

## Assets

### Browser icon "time-clock-fire"

| | |
|---|---|
| Title | "time-clock-fire", from the "Ultimate color icons" set |
| Author | Streamline |
| Source | https://icon-sets.iconify.design/streamline-ultimate-color/time-clock-fire/ (the set is published at https://github.com/webalys-hq/streamline-vectors) |
| Retrieved | 2026-10-06, from Iconify |
| License | Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0): https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ |
| Copyright notice | None supplied by the licensor |
| Warranty | Provided as is, without warranties; see section 5 of the license |
| Used for | The app's browser tab icon (favicon) and iOS home screen icon |
| Files | `frontend/public/favicon.svg`, `frontend/public/favicon.ico`, `frontend/public/apple-touch-icon.png` |

Changes made to the original icon:

1. `favicon.svg`: the `width` and `height` attributes were changed from `1em` to `24`, and a header
   comment with this credit was added. The `viewBox`, the shapes and the colors are unchanged.
2. `favicon.ico`: the SVG was rendered at 16, 32 and 48 pixels and packed into one ICO file (a
   change of format).
3. `apple-touch-icon.png`: the SVG was rendered at 144 pixels and centered on an opaque white
   180 x 180 pixel square (a change of format and an added background).

The two files in 2 and 3 can be regenerated from the SVG, from the repository root:

```shell
for n in 16 32 48; do rsvg-convert -w $n -h $n frontend/public/favicon.svg -o $n.png; done
magick 16.png 32.png 48.png frontend/public/favicon.ico
rsvg-convert -w 144 -h 144 frontend/public/favicon.svg -o 144.png
magick -size 180x180 xc:white 144.png -gravity center -composite \
  -background white -alpha remove -alpha off PNG24:frontend/public/apple-touch-icon.png
```

### Country flags "circle-flags"

| | |
|---|---|
| Title | "circle-flags", a collection of circular SVG flags |
| Author | HatScripts |
| Source | https://github.com/HatScripts/circle-flags, commit `379588b5da95482d6bbf10bd45644a35b0609ea6` (2026-07-26) |
| Retrieved | 2026-10-14, from GitHub |
| License | MIT License: https://github.com/HatScripts/circle-flags/blob/master/LICENSE.md |
| Copyright notice | "Copyright (c) 2026 HatScripts" |
| Warranty | Provided "as is", without warranty of any kind; see the last paragraph of the license |
| Used for | The flag next to each country in the country picker on the company, address and bank address forms |
| Files | `frontend/public/flags/*.svg` (one per ISO 3166-1 alpha-2 country, 249 files) and `frontend/public/flags/LICENSE` (the license text, as MIT requires it to accompany the copies) |

Changes made to the original: none to any file's content. Only the 249 ISO country flags were
copied, not the set's subdivision, language or other flags. Six of those codes are symbolic links
upstream to another flag (`bq` to `bq-bo`, `bv` and `sj` to `no`, `hm` to `au`, `sh` to `sh-hl`,
`um` to `us`) and were copied as the file each link points to. The SVGs carry no credit comment
of their own, so that they stay identical to upstream and can be refreshed by copying them again;
the license file in the same folder carries the notice instead.

